Z||000026||Old Lar||02-17-2001||01:20 PM||||At one point in time you could order a car built the way you wanted it.  You just waited for assembly.  I did that in 76 with a Chevy Nova.  Set up a four door with 350 4bbl, Camaro sport suspension variable power steering and vinyl interior, with a 2.73 POSI rear end. I wanted a car that was set for highway driving not drag strip. (married at that time).  It was one of the most reliable cars that could cruise at 70 all day and not even breath hard. I imagine that some Fieros could have been ordered rather stripped, although the dealers would rather load them up for profit markup on the options. My 87 was a dealer order, that had every option available including subwoofer system..  He had a bunch of them on the lot when I found it, every color imaginable with either auto or 5 spd transmission.  My 88 was a Florida car with a plain top, with all the power equipment, leather seats, but the base am-fm cassette radio.<P>Sometimes they are built with whatever equipment is available at the time of assembly.  I had  Chrysler product special ordered, however when they were building it, they did not have the engine available, so they substituted a different engine.  I refused to accept it. The dealer talked me into another order, and that car came in with the wrong interior.  Waisted 6 months with Chrysler trying to get a car.  Haven't looked at another Chrysler in 20 years.<P>Sorry to ramble. Crooks in the auto industry.  I had to take the dealer to arbitration to get my deposit back.  I did and got a Pontiac.||||reg||3
Z||000027||Phil||02-17-2001||01:52 PM||||I got an 88 coupe t-top and the only option on it was A/C ||||reg||1
